 "notice": "Photographs and scans of Code 128 labels from Wikimedia Commons. Each file has its own author and licence, listed with it, and its file page on Commons.",
 "selection": "Photographs and scans of real Code 128 labels, not renderings, taken from Commons in November 2026: every file in Category:Code 128 and Category:GS1-128, and 54 of the 135 files with an allowed licence in Category:Barcode and its regional and street-light subcategories, picked by title and description. A photo is kept when its file page gives CC0, CC BY 4.0 or a public-domain tag, it is a baseline JPEG, it shows one Code 128 symbol (or several with the same text), and a printed line gives that symbol's whole text. The Code 128 symbol's `text` is that line as read by eye, without the spaces it is grouped by and without the parentheses around GS1 application identifiers. The bars were counted on ten of the photos to check the symbology and the length; the 13-character postal numbers take 43 or 49 bars, which leaves no room for spaces. Not counted: FlagTag, which is too slanted, and two of the three Zlin lamp tags, which are the same label as the third. Left out: CC BY-SA and CC BY 2.0 files; progressive JPEGs (the Oatly GS1-128 label, the Tucheng registered-mail sticker, the Slovak vignettes); labels with two Code 128 symbols of different text (the DHL Paeckchen labels, the UPS label, phone boxes); labels whose printed line does not give the symbol's text (Chinese rail tickets, the DHL delivery notes, the four ski and cable-car tickets looked at); labels whose bar count shows Code 39 (the 2006 Deutsche Post registration label, the Rokycany street lights, the BSB library card, the M.2 screw bag, the DCMA tool tag); Jordan Post type PO1A, whose last letter cannot be told from a zero and whose S10 check digit does not match its printed number; the Rapoo KX box label, where O and 0 cannot be told apart; and renderings (KUNHM, PIATS, Leclerc Drive).",
 "truth": "Every symbol each photo shows, looked at in November 2026: besides the Code 128 symbol, a QR code on each Zlin lamp tag, an Aztec code on the deposit voucher, an Interleaved 2 of 5 symbol on the DHL label and covered bars on FlagTag that may be a symbol, whose texts were not read. The corners of each Code 128 symbol were placed by eye on magnified views at the same time.",
